# EcoSuit MK.I — Step-in process
**Rear-entry hatch. You do not climb in through the neck. You step in, lock the hatch, then live.**
Paper procedure. Assumes ASSY-CHEST, HUT, exo, plates, CUP-SM, and FTL-BH-1 / DSH-1 exist as separate LRUs already built.

---

## 0. What “step-in” means on this suit

EcoSuit is a hard-shell HUT with an internal exo and overlapping ceramic-hemp plates. The pressure path is rear-entry, not waist-disconnect and not helmet-first.

| Item | State for step-in |
|---|---|
| Rear hatch | Open, parked on the dorsal latch or suit-up stand |
| Dorsal pack (FTL-BH-1 / DSH-1) | Off the hatch ring, or swung aside on the stand hinge |
| Helmet | Off or hinged open. Never the entry hole |
| Pauldrons / chest plates | On. They do not come off to don |
| CUP-SM + cap | Installed. Cap on. No module swap during don |
| SEAs | Clutch OPEN (free) |
| V-EBM plate latches | Inhibited (air / dirty vac) |
| DEAs | Off |
| Bladder / LCVG | Crew wears LCVG. Bladder is in the suit |

You step backward or sideways onto the stand, feet into the legs, hips into the yoke, arms into the sleeves, back through the hatch opening. Hatch closes onto the ring. Pack goes on last.

---

## 1. Hardware that makes step-in possible

Build these before you write a donning card.

1. **Rear hatch ring** on the HUT — dual seal, four pack bolts, Datum C.
2. **Hatch door** — swings up or aside on the stand; does not dangle on plates.
3. **Suit-up stand** — holds the suit at 15–25° aft lean, hatch at scapula height, feet free of the floor by ~50–80 mm so the crew does not fight 1 g fabric.
4. **Leg tunnels** — open enough for a booted LCVG foot without scraping the knee convolute.
5. **Yoke** — pelvic ring is the seat. Crew sits into it, they do not hang from the hatch.
6. **Sleeve line** — arms go in after hips are seated, or the hatch lip skins the deltoid.
7. **Pack hinge or trolley** — FTL-BH-1 never manhandled across a ceramic facet.
8. **Dead-face** — pack off = PWR-1 and HV open, COOL QDs shut.

If the stand is missing, you do not have a step-in suit. You have a costume people fall out of.

