## 2. Pre-don states (T-20 min)

| Check | Pass |
|---|---|
| Suit on stand, hatch open, pack off or swung | Visual |
| Internal exo clear, no tools in the yoke | Visual |
| SEA clutches OPEN, brakes off | Indicator + hand-backdrive |
| V-EBM HV inhibit | Lamp / breaker open |
| CUP-SM cap on, no service lines hanging into the bore | Visual |
| LCVG on crew, dry, comms cap or bio harness as spec | Crew |
| Bladder dry, no fold across the hatch land | Visual |
| Plate family serial matches traveler | Tag |
| Helmet and gloves staged, not in the hatch path | Staged |
| Loop fluids filled, but pack not mated | QD caps on |

Do not start step-in with a powered knee. A closing SEA during don is a broken femur.

