## 3. Step-in sequence (1 g stand)

Count is one crew + one suit tech. IVA can drop the tech if the stand is vehicle-mounted and the hatch is overhead.

### 3.1 Feet
1. Crew stands on the step plate behind the suit.
2. Left foot into left leg tunnel, toes pointed, knee slightly flexed.
3. Right foot.
4. Do not lock the ankle convolute yet. Boots find the footbed.

### 3.2 Hips
5. Sit back into the pelvic yoke. Weight goes into EXO-TI / EXO-SG, not into a chest plate.
6. Tech confirms the yoke has the iliac crest, not the lumbar hanging on the hatch lip.
7. Close any waist restraint that is *not* the pressure seal.

### 3.3 Arms
8. Left arm through the sleeve. Shoulder SEA free.
9. Right arm.
10. Hands find the glove disconnects but gloves stay off until hatch is sealed (or per vehicle card — pick one and freeze it).

### 3.4 Spine and hatch
11. Crew leans forward onto the HUT. Sternum cup faces Datum A. No shove on CAP-S.
12. Tech swings the hatch. Dual seals on the ring. No fabric in the land.
13. Hatch latches: mechanical first, then witness.
14. Pressure check of the hatch cavity per vehicle card (or leave for cabin pump later — freeze one).

### 3.5 Pack
15. Swing / trolley FTL-BH-1 onto the four hatch bolts.
16. Torque star pattern. Witness.
17. Mate COOL QDs, then PWR-1, then TM. HV stays inhibited until vacuum interlock.
18. Heat-pipe stub to the chest cup seated.

### 3.6 Head, hands, power-up
19. Helmet on neck ring. Lock. Visor per card.
20. Gloves on.
21. Comms / bio check.
22. SEA power: still OPEN until the crew says they are planted.
23. Brief impedance check on a stand, 1 g, no tools.
24. V-EBM remains inhibited until a gauge says hard vacuum.

Step-in is over when hatch + pack + helmet + gloves are locked and the crew can stand off the step plate without the suit walking away from them.

