## 5. Step-out (reverse, with two extra rules)

1. SEAs OPEN. Confirm backdrive.
2. HV inhibit. Cap latches passive.
3. Gloves off, helmet off.
4. Pack dead-face, QDs, unbolt, swing aside.
5. Hatch open.
6. Arms out, then stand up out of the yoke, then feet.
7. Crew never pulls themselves out by a chest plate or the sternum cap.
8. If the cup over-temp or dose flag is set, pack and hatch as normal, then treat the SM as a hot LRU on the stand — do not yank CAP-S with a bare hand because the card said “90 s.”

---

## 6. What must already be true of the chest article

From the chest-plate traveler, step-in inherits:

- Plates stay on during don. No “remove plastron to enter.”
- Cup stays in. No module swap mid-don.
- Coolant and power run along superior longerons to the hatch, not across a plate bond, so the pack can mate without flexing a sandwich.
- Spider takes Case A. The crew sitting into the yoke is a nothing-load compared with 6 g, but only if they sit into the yoke.

If any of those is false, stop. You are not stepping into EcoSuit. You are climbing into a broken dummy.

---

## 7. Timing gates (acceptance)

| Action | Gate |
|---|---|
| Feet to seated in yoke | ≤ 30 s, no binding |
| Arms in | ≤ 20 s |
| Hatch close + latch | ≤ 20 s |
| Pack on + QDs + PWR-1 | ≤ 90 s |
| Helmet + gloves | ≤ 60 s |
| Full step-in, 1 g, two-person | ≤ 4 min first article; tighten later |
| Emergency hatch open + pack dead-face | ≤ 30 s |

If the crew needs a third person to aim a foot, the stand angle or the leg tunnel is wrong. Do not “train through” a geometry fault.

---

## 8. Inhibits during step-in (non-negotiable)

| System | During step-in | After lock, still in air | After vacuum interlock |
|---|---|---|---|
| SEA | OPEN | OPEN or HOLD | Impedance when the card says walk |
| V-EBM | HV off | HV off | Armed only if gauge is hard-vac |
| DEA | Off | Off | Off until glove card |
| PWR-1 to cup | Unmated until pack is on | On if loop is up | On |
| PWR-HV | Open | Open | Per latch card |
| Real ABH-2600 | Not in the suit | Not in the suit | Not in the suit |

