## 9. Failure modes this procedure exists to prevent

| Failure | Cause | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Entry through the neck | Treating it like a soft suit | Torn bladder, smashed visor |
| SEA powered | “Help the crew in” | Locked joint, injury |
| Pack dragged over tiles | No trolley | Chipped CER-B, scrap plate |
| Weight on CAP-S | Crew leans on the artwork | Cup land crush, hemp bore exposed |
| Fabric in hatch land | Rushed close | Leak you find at 3 psi |
| HV on in the booth | “Test the latches” | Paschen / shock |
| Step-in without a stand | Heroics | Missed footbed, convolute damage |
| REAL-core in the cup | Wrong object | Tide / g FAIL-CLOSED — not a donning issue, a design crime |

---

## 10. First-article donning test

1. Dummy HUT + chest article + one leg pair + hatch + pack mass analog.
2. Two subjects, three runs each, 1 g stand.
3. Record times, hang-ups, plate contact, hatch-seal debris.
4. One run with SEA “accidentally” armed — confirm the card stops the run.
5. Freeze stand angle, tunnel trim, and pack-last order before a full suit set.

Title block:
- Step-in is rear hatch, pack last, SEAs open.
- Chest plates and CUP-SM stay on.
- FTL-BH-1 is the dorsal service pack, not an entry hatch.
- ABH-2600-SM only. ABH-2600-REAL is not worn.